      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "UBETONRED (9) has been racing well of late and kept the good form rolling last time when 4.5 metres from the winner in fourth over 1780m at Redcliffe. Good enough to put himself in the winners' stall in what might just be the right race now. TREACHEROUS BELLE (5) finished fifth last time out, beaten 6 metres, in a far better performance at this track over 1660m. Recent efforts are good enough to take out a race like this. MISS BAY KING COLE (10) is right in contention after finishing in the placings for the second time in a row last start, beaten 7 metres into third at this track. No reason she cannot take this out and LOCHINVAR JEWELLS (2) must be included on the back of some solid recent form. Solid most recently when fifth at Redcliffe over 2040m.",
